ent-harness/docs/` is correct. |\\n\\n## Key Links (wiring)\\n\\n| Link | Status | Evidence |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Doc listed in meta-docs index | WIRED | `skills/dh-meta-docs/SKILL.md:25` names the doc explicitly. |\\n| `agents/backlog-item-groomer.md` \\u2192 doc | WIRED | `:429` \\u2014 \\\"load `dh:dh-meta-docs` and read\\\" the Backlog Item Groomed Schema. |\\n| `skills/groom-backlog-item/references/groomer-agent.md` \\u2192 doc | WIRED | `:33` and `:74` dispatch prompts route via `dh:dh-meta-docs`. |\\n| `KNOWN_ENTITIES.md:355` `L64\\u201381` citation | STILL VALID | Net line delta of the fix is 0 (6 ins / 6 del), so the Groomed Sections table remains at 64\\u201381. The deferred R4 spot-check resolves clean. |\\n\\n## Anti-Goal Compliance\\n\\n| Anti-Goal | Violated | Evidence |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Touch `templates/backlog-item.md` | NO | Last touched by `20c84f3b5` (#3330), not by this fix. |\\n| Modify `## Groomed` section table | NO | No diff hunk in that range; table intact at `:62-81`. |\\n| Modify the `:58` \\\"No line numbers\\\" rule | NO | Intact at `:58`. |\\n| Modify the Issue #314 condition | NO | Intact at `:80`. |\\n| Re-add `name` as legacy alias | NO | Zero field-reference hits. |\\n| Add `reference:` to frontmatter | NO | Absent from the example. |\\n\\n## Gaps\\n\\n1. **Edit 2 introduces a fresh, false API citation \\u2014 `backlog_groom(groomed_content=...)`.**\\n\\n   The new `:5` Scope paragraph asserts groomed content is \\\"passed through `backlog_groom(groomed_content=...)`\\\". That parameter does not exist. `backlog_core/server.py:2550` defines `backlog_groom(ctx, selector, section, content, entry_id, replace_section, reason, append, sections, mark_groomed)`. A dedicated regression test asserts its absence \\u2014 `tests/test_backlog_core_server.py:1649-1656`, `assert \\\"groomed_content\\\" not in sig.parameters` \\u2014 and it passes (`1 passed in 15.83s`).\\n\\n   This is the same defect class #3332 exists to eliminate: a non-existent field/parameter name presented to an agent as the current interface, in agent-facing instruction content reachable by all three live consumers. An agent following it emits a call that raises `TypeError`. The real write path is `backlog_groom(selector=..., section=..., content=...)` or `sections={...}`.\\n\\n   Origin is upstream of implementation: the phrasing came from the item description, was carried verbatim into the architect spec's Edit 2 replacement text, and T1 applied it verbatim as its constraints required. Not an implementation defect \\u2014 a spec defect that the six ACs do not cover, so no AC catches it.\\n\\n## Remediation Path\\n\\n1. **Correct the `:5` API citation** \\u2014 replace `backlog_groom(groomed_content=...)` with the real call form (`backlog_groom(section=..., content=...)`), or drop the parenthetical entirely since the paragraph's point is the content/storage boundary, not the call signature. One-line edit to the same file, same scope.\\n\\n## Quality Gates\\n\\n| Gate | Result | Output |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Targeted regression test | PASS | `test_backlog_groom_no_groomed_content_param` \\u2014 1 passed in 15.83s (run as evidence for the gap, not as a feature gate). |\\n| Live delivery surface validation | SKIPPED | No `.dh/language-manifest.yaml` in the repo; `quality_gates.live_validation` is undeclared. |\\n| Prose test surface | N/A | Documentation-only change; nothing in CI reads this file. Grep + primary-source read is the entire verification surface. |\\n\\n## LIVE_VALIDATION\\n\\n```\\nLIVE_VALIDATION: SKIPPED \\u2014 no live_validation command declared in language manifest.\\nAdd quality_gates.live_validation to your .dh/language-manifest.yaml to enable live delivery surface validation.\\n```\\n\\n## Concerns (observed, out of scope)\\n\\n- `:170` and `:209` still show `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/...` paths inside the Example Groomed Body. They are illustrative resource references, not storage assertions, so AC #3/#4 hold \\u2014